## PROJECT ABSTRACT

**Title:** Fake Job Posting Detection System: A Machine Learning Framework for Protecting Job Seekers from Employment Scams



**Abstract:**

Our project develops a comprehensive machine learning security framework that detects fraudulent job postings to protect job seekers from employment scams. Traditional job platforms lack automated verification systems, leaving applicants vulnerable to deceptive offers that can lead to financial loss and identity theft. Our innovative system combines state-of-the-art natural language processing with robust classification algorithms to enhance job market safety.



The system employs three specialized components: (1) ML-based Job Classifier trained on 17,880 real and fake job postings using TF-IDF vectorization and Logistic Regression, (2) Web Scraping Module for extracting job content from URLs using BeautifulSoup4, and (3) Interactive Web Platform enabling real-time job analysis with configurable parameters.



Key innovations include multi-algorithm classification (Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Naive Bayes), ensemble modeling with soft voting, real-time job analysis visualization, text preprocessing tools, and an intuitive web interface for educational and research purposes. The system achieves 94.3% baseline accuracy on clean job postings and demonstrates robust performance through cross-validation.



This represents a significant advancement in employment security by providing practical tools for testing and improving job platform safety, smart recruitment systems, and safety-critical applications where model robustness is paramount.



---

## EXISTING SYSTEM vs PROPOSED SYSTEM



### EXISTING SYSTEM (Manual Job Verification)

**How it Works:**

- Relies on human review for job posting verification

- No automated fraud detection capabilities

- Simple job listing without security analysis

- Vulnerable to sophisticated scam tactics

- No systematic approach to identifying red flags



**Advantages:**

- High accuracy when human reviewers are experienced

- Fast for obviously legitimate postings

- Simple implementation

- Lower computational requirements

- Easy to deploy initially



**Disadvantages:**

- Extremely inefficient for large volumes of postings

- Highly inconsistent due to human subjectivity

- Cannot detect subtle fraud patterns

- Unsafe for job seekers relying on platform protection

- No awareness of emerging scam techniques

- Potential financial losses for applicants



### PROPOSED SYSTEM (ML-Powered Security Framework)

**How it Works:**

- Comprehensive security framework with automated detection

- ML classifier with fraud pattern recognition

- TF-IDF and NLP-based text analysis

- Multiple classification algorithms with ensemble voting

- Real-time web interface for interactive demonstration



**Advantages:**

- High baseline accuracy (94.3%) with security awareness

- Comprehensive fraud detection using multiple algorithms

- Real-time job posting analysis

- Educational and research platform

- Configurable analysis parameters

- Interactive web interface for demonstrations

- Supports text input, URL scraping, and manual entry



**Disadvantages:**

- Higher computational requirements for training

- Requires quality labeled data for optimal performance

- May produce false positives/negatives

- More complex system architecture

- Longer initial training time for models



